// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! power.resource's functions: what the machine can do about its own
//! power, turning it off, and who is told when its power button is
//! pressed. A resource: no Open or Close, its first function in the first
//! slot. The base comes from OpenResource("power.resource").
##include libs/exec/exec as exec
##include resources/power as power
##basetype PowerBase
##name power.resource
##bias 0
##public
/// What this machine can do about its own power (POWERF_*); 0 where it
/// can do nothing.
u32 PowerAbilities()
/// The machine turned off. It returns only where that could not be done.
void PowerOff()
/// `signals` sent to `task` when the machine's power button is pressed;
/// null on a machine with no such button, or without memory.
?*power.PowerNotify AddPowerNotify(*exec.Task task, u32 signals)
/// No more of that.
void RemPowerNotify(?*power.PowerNotify notify)
##end
